  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization for imposition of additional sales tax in the county of Otsego",
    "basePrintNo": "S3537",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3537-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3537\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending\nthe authorization for imposition of additional sales tax in the county\nof Otsego\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Otsego County Board of Representatives to impose an\nadditional one percent sales tax for a two year period\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 1210 of the tax law to extend the\nauthorization for Otsego County to impose an additional one percent\n(1%) sales tax until November 30, 2017. Section two provides the\neffective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe law expires on November 30, 2015.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Otsego County Board of Representatives has approved a resolution\n(No. 52-20150107) requesting that the New York State Legislature\nintroduce and enact a bill to authorize the county to impose an\nadditional one percent sales and use tax for the period through\nNovember 30, 2017.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThe law was previously extended by Chapter 317 of the laws of 2013 (S.\n4018/A.6050).\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediate\n\n",
